# FreeBSD system calls behind std's kernel operations (the operation list of
# library/std/os/platform/unix/linux/syscalls/operations.sn, which names OS
# services, not one kernel): <operation> <SYS_ name> [fallback SYS_ name ...]
# FreeBSD numbers its system calls once for every architecture
# (sys/kern/syscalls.master -> sys/sys/syscall.h), so there is one table.
# The FreeBSD call is the one that provides the service; where its
# arguments differ from the Linux call of the same row, the std code that
# issues it on FreeBSD says so (fstatat, getdirentries, __getcwd, wait4,
# fork, getrlimit/setrlimit).
# "-" marks an operation FreeBSD lacks. Its number is 0xFFFFFFFF, past the
# system-call table: the kernel would answer with nosys, which raises
# SIGSYS, so std never issues such an operation on FreeBSD.
قراءة read
كتابة write
إغلاق close
فتح_عند openat
# statx is Linux only; std's FreeBSD metadata reads struct stat (fstatat).
إحصاء_مسار -
معلومات_ملف_عند fstatat
